Z||000005||Hank is Here||09-25-2001||12:18 AM||||I am a fan of bigger is better.<BR>Seriously how much does a dually diesel pickup and trailer cost?  Maybe 15 G or so.  <P>I plan on just buying a International rollback with wheellift.  Their life is about 600,000 miles for a small one and 1,000,000 for a medium sized truck.  You can haul two cars or whatever you need with about 19 feet of deck space.  I have seen them for as low as 9G with medium mileage 400,000 or so but would look for a few less miles like 250,000.  All I would do then is just reconstruct the truck by "removing" a rear spring to lessen the GVW for less registration costs.  I have used rollbacks for moving everything.  Also they are really nice for gardening  ie: removing shrubs trees ect. with the winch.<BR>One truck would last me 20 year or so and the cost over time would be minimal.  Think about it, it is not as crazy as first seems!   ||||reg||1
